-- title:
--   Commuting With GIncomplete Of Complete
-- statement:
--   **Commuting with the incomplete part is inherited from the complete-part bounds.**
--
--   Let `params` be LIDT parameters, let $\psi_{bi}$ be a bipartite state, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. If `hcomm` supplies `CommutingWithGCompleteStatement` for errors $\gamma$ and $\zeta$, then the corresponding incomplete-part package exists:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{CommutingWithGIncompleteStatement}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},\gamma,\zeta).
--   $$
--
--   Both fields have error `commutingWithGIncompleteError`, equal to the complete-part bound
--
--   $$
--   36m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The result replaces a complete factor by its complementary effect and transfers the same squared-distance bound.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commutingWithGIncomplete_ofComplete`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
